(465772, 43948, 3102, '<td valign="top">NOW we''re talkin''!  :)  Very nicely done -- great skin tones and a great, clean background.</td>', 'NOW we''re talkin''!  :)  Very nicely done -- great skin tones and a great, clean background.', '2003-10-29 11:09:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(465777, 44389, 6845, '<td valign="top">Very interesting take on the challenge. Even more interesting way to show it. My only problem is that i must assume that she is doing this gracefully :) I like the motion blur and the composition.</td>', 'Very interesting take on the challenge. Even more interesting way to show it. My only problem is that i must assume that she is doing this gracefully :) I like the motion blur and the composition.', '2003-10-29 11:10:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(465778, 43737, 7369, '<td valign="top">It''s a pity that the photo is out of focus. Maybe that''s because there was too little light (the shutter time was too long for handholding?).</td>', 'It''s a pity that the photo is out of focus. Maybe that''s because there was too little light (the shutter time was too long for handholding?).', '2003-10-29 11:10:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(465779, 43962, 6845, '<td valign="top">Looks like it could use a little more resolution. Nice subject, light and composition.</td>', 'Looks like it could use a little more resolution. Nice subject, light and composition.', '2003-10-29 11:11:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(465784, 44318, 12882, '<td valign="top">very nice</td>', 'very nice', '2003-10-29 11:16:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(465789, 44333, 8522, '<td valign="top">Big shame about the orange colour cast from using the wrong white balance, and the glare off the window. Compositionally this doesn''t quite work for me... I personally would have stepped back a little to place her in the right half of the shot, and make sure I didn''t chop her toes off. This way, you would also see more of the  texture of the crumbling wall on the left. The shot feels like it needs a little rotation so the vertical lines are vertical. I do however like the mood and atmosphere of this photo. 5</td>', 'Big shame about the orange colour cast from using the wrong white balance, and the glare off the window. Compositionally this doesn''t quite work for me... I personally would have stepped back a little to place her in the right half of the shot, and make sure I didn''t chop her toes off. This way, you would also see more of the  texture of the crumbling wall on the left. The shot feels like it needs a little rotation so the vertical lines are vertical. I do however like the mood and atmosphere of this photo. 5', '2003-10-29 11:22:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(465792, 44249, 8522, '<td valign="top">Great shot from what I can make out... next time make sure the image is a bit larger! 6</td>', 'Great shot from what I can make out... next time make sure the image is a bit larger! 6', '2003-10-29 11:24:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(465798, 43451, 10858, '<td valign="top">I really like this idea, anyway I would have left just as much space from the cross on the top, as you left on the sides, and I think it''s a little bit noisy, too.</td>', 'I really like this idea, anyway I would have left just as much space from the cross on the top, as you left on the sides, and I think it''s a little bit noisy, too.', '2003-10-29 11:27:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(465802, 43636, 10858, '<td valign="top">I like this subject a much! :-) Anyway, it''s a bit too blurry for me, I would have used a simpler and more homogenic background to highlight the Mantis, and the lighting is also a bit glaring for me above him.</td>', 'I like this subject a much! :-) Anyway, it''s a bit too blurry for me, I would have used a simpler and more homogenic background to highlight the Mantis, and the lighting is also a bit glaring for me above him.', '2003-10-29 11:30:36.000000', NULL, 1),
