(466255, 44314, 772, '<td valign="top">The pink border adds a bit too much to the chaos of the image.</td>', 'The pink border adds a bit too much to the chaos of the image.', '2003-10-29 16:12:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(466256, 44280, 3087, '<td valign="top">The lighting really makes the rose glow and I like how it separates the bud from the stem. Nice use of negative space though it does make me think of a florists message car with space for a scribbled note from the sender!</td>', 'The lighting really makes the rose glow and I like how it separates the bud from the stem. Nice use of negative space though it does make me think of a florists message car with space for a scribbled note from the sender!', '2003-10-29 16:12:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(466257, 44143, 772, '<td valign="top">beautiful orchid.. i would have leveled out the background to make it completely black and not let the lace patterns show through...</td>', 'beautiful orchid.. i would have leveled out the background to make it completely black and not let the lace patterns show through...', '2003-10-29 16:13:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(466258, 44303, 772, '<td valign="top">i love the way the color leftover in this image draws my attention away from the subject of the shot ;)</td>', 'i love the way the color leftover in this image draws my attention away from the subject of the shot ;)', '2003-10-29 16:15:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(466260, 44309, 2223, '<td valign="top">Funky, i like it. I would like to know how you did this.</td>', 'Funky, i like it. I would like to know how you did this.', '2003-10-29 16:16:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(466263, 44307, 12857, '<td valign="top">I FIGURED THERE WOULD BE MANY PHOTOGRAPHS OF STATUES.  THIS  ONE HAS A GREAT FEEL TO IT.  WONDERFUL PHOTO.   GREAT CHOICE FOR BLACK AND WHITE.</td>', 'I FIGURED THERE WOULD BE MANY PHOTOGRAPHS OF STATUES.  THIS  ONE HAS A GREAT FEEL TO IT.  WONDERFUL PHOTO.   GREAT CHOICE FOR BLACK AND WHITE.', '2003-10-29 16:17:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(466264, 44437, 3087, '<td valign="top">A beautiful image but focus just seems too soft to me, or perhaps it''s because focus is on the mist and not on the shrubbery in the foreground?</td>', 'A beautiful image but focus just seems too soft to me, or perhaps it''s because focus is on the mist and not on the shrubbery in the foreground?', '2003-10-29 16:19:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(466266, 43948, 3087, '<td valign="top">Nicely taken. pose creates a pleasing composition, model''s facial expression doesn''t look too forced, boa adds right touch of colour. Not sure it shows grace as much as flesh on offer but it''s a well taken image!</td>', 'Nicely taken. pose creates a pleasing composition, model''s facial expression doesn''t look too forced, boa adds right touch of colour. Not sure it shows grace as much as flesh on offer but it''s a well taken image!', '2003-10-29 16:21:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(466268, 43554, 13306, '<td valign="top">The picture has something like personal charm which catches one''s attention (10p.)</td>', 'The picture has something like personal charm which catches one''s attention (10p.)', '2003-10-29 16:22:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(466271, 44374, 3087, '<td valign="top">A pretty silhouette which shows the graceful form of simple grasses but the image lacks that extra punch that would make it something special - perhaps a real focal point?</td>', 'A pretty silhouette which shows the graceful form of simple grasses but the image lacks that extra punch that would make it something special - perhaps a real focal point?', '2003-10-29 16:24:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(466273, 44318, 3087, '<td valign="top">Beautiful colours and light. The curving shapes remind me very much of a forest I used to play in during childhood and even of a favourite photograph taken when I received my first SLR camera aged about 11 or 12. I wish I could find the negative! The dark line of the curved bows above and the foremost trunk at the left create a beautiful framing and the unbroken carpet of leaves feels very peaceful.</td>', 'Beautiful colours and light. The curving shapes remind me very much of a forest I used to play in during childhood and even of a favourite photograph taken when I received my first SLR camera aged about 11 or 12. I wish I could find the negative! The dark line of the curved bows above and the foremost trunk at the left create a beautiful framing and the unbroken carpet of leaves feels very peaceful.', '2003-10-29 16:27:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(466275, 43436, 3087, '<td valign="top">I''m not sure that I see grace here but since it''s something that''s very much in the eye of the beholder I''m certainly not saying "this doesn''t meet the challenge".<br/>I really like this image very much and it reminds me of work I''ve seen hanging in the National Portrait Gallery here in London - I can''t recall the name of the photographers but a couple created series of candid prints portraying real people going about their real lives. I like the high contrast, the strong lines and the composition created by the lines of the buildings and position of the boy.</td>', 'I''m not sure that I see grace here but since it''s something that''s very much in the eye of the beholder I''m certainly not saying "this doesn''t meet the challenge".I really like this image very much and it reminds me of work I''ve seen hanging in the National Portrait Gallery here in London - I can''t recall the name of the photographers but a couple created series of candid prints portraying real people going about their real lives. I like the high contrast, the strong lines and the composition created by the lines of the buildings and position of the boy.', '2003-10-29 16:29:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(466276, 44285, 3087, '<td valign="top">I adore this. It creates a feeling of peace and euphoria that I can''t quite explain - something about the soft merging of shades of purple, the beauty of the drops of water, some in sharp focus and others not, and the diagonal line fading into fuzziness at the top corner. I don''t know how many will agree with me but this is certainly my favourite entry of the challenge.</td>', 'I adore this. It creates a feeling of peace and euphoria that I can''t quite explain - something about the soft merging of shades of purple, the beauty of the drops of water, some in sharp focus and others not, and the diagonal line fading into fuzziness at the top corner. I don''t know how many will agree with me but this is certainly my favourite entry of the challenge.', '2003-10-29 16:32:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(466277, 44307, 3087, '<td valign="top">What an unusual viewpoint and choice of what to include! I like it! Not sure about the high contrast - is the image posterised? Do like the inclusion of the windows at top right.</td>', 'What an unusual viewpoint and choice of what to include! I like it! Not sure about the high contrast - is the image posterised? Do like the inclusion of the windows at top right.', '2003-10-29 16:36:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(466278, 44189, 3087, '<td valign="top">Beautifully done, the low DOF on the background really allows one to concentrate on the warmth of the greens and see their variety without being distracted by harsh shapes. The leaf itself is beautiful (I assume it''s one of those artificial ones sold by decoration stores?) and the composition of the overall image works very well with the diagonal of the stem pushing out from one of the corners.</td>', 'Beautifully done, the low DOF on the background really allows one to concentrate on the warmth of the greens and see their variety without being distracted by harsh shapes. The leaf itself is beautiful (I assume it''s one of those artificial ones sold by decoration stores?) and the composition of the overall image works very well with the diagonal of the stem pushing out from one of the corners.', '2003-10-29 16:37:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(466279, 43994, 3087, '<td valign="top">An interesting juxtaposition of soft nature and harsh man made object. Although the black and white really allows for the forms and shadows to come through I wonder if colour would bring out the contrast between warm vibrant leaf colours and cold fence?</td>', 'An interesting juxtaposition of soft nature and harsh man made object. Although the black and white really allows for the forms and shadows to come through I wonder if colour would bring out the contrast between warm vibrant leaf colours and cold fence?', '2003-10-29 16:39:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(466280, 43996, 3087, '<td valign="top">Has a Monet quality to the background. A little too static in composition but an interesting image.</td>', 'Has a Monet quality to the background. A little too static in composition but an interesting image.', '2003-10-29 16:40:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(466283, 44261, 3087, '<td valign="top">Interesting variation on the droplet theme - I really like the non-symmetrical background and the way the petal pierces the water surface and interrupts the circular pattern of water. The colours are good too.</td>', 'Interesting variation on the droplet theme - I really like the non-symmetrical background and the way the petal pierces the water surface and interrupts the circular pattern of water. The colours are good too.', '2003-10-29 16:42:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(466289, 44127, 3087, '<td valign="top">A beautiful leaf and great composition.<br/>My two suggestions would be:<br/>The leaf is so uniform in colour that this macro treatment doesn''t bring out as much interesting detail as it might - I wonder if a leaf with more variations of orange, yellow and even maroon might be more interesting?<br/>The water looks a little messy - would it have been possible to dry the leaf off and then add a few droplets manually that retained their droplet shape?<br/>You may have been striving for a more natural feeling of wetness of course, in which case my suggestion is of no interest.<br/></td>', 'A beautiful leaf and great composition.My two suggestions would be:The leaf is so uniform in colour that this macro treatment doesn''t bring out as much interesting detail as it might - I wonder if a leaf with more variations of orange, yellow and even maroon might be more interesting?The water looks a little messy - would it have been possible to dry the leaf off and then add a few droplets manually that retained their droplet shape?You may have been striving for a more natural feeling of wetness of course, in which case my suggestion is of no interest.', '2003-10-29 16:47:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(466290, 44459, 3087, '<td valign="top">I find the border particularly unpleasant to the extent that it does lessen my enjoyment of the image.<br/>Ignoring it for the moment I like the image quite a lot - the simplicity and the studio rather than natural background works well. In terms of composition I''d like a touch more space above and less below.</td>', 'I find the border particularly unpleasant to the extent that it does lessen my enjoyment of the image.Ignoring it for the moment I like the image quite a lot - the simplicity and the studio rather than natural background works well. In terms of composition I''d like a touch more space above and less below.', '2003-10-29 16:49:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(466292, 44400, 3087, '<td valign="top">Beautiful - a wonderful portrait of a fallen leaf - I like the composition, the shape and shadows, the angle within the frame, the warm black and white tone. An absolutely wonderful entry, one of my favourites in this challenge.</td>', 'Beautiful - a wonderful portrait of a fallen leaf - I like the composition, the shape and shadows, the angle within the frame, the warm black and white tone. An absolutely wonderful entry, one of my favourites in this challenge.', '2003-10-29 16:51:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(466306, 44432, 13342, '<td valign="top">I think this is a very artistic interpretation of "Grace". Great Job.</td>', 'I think this is a very artistic interpretation of "Grace". Great Job.', '2003-10-29 17:04:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(466307, 44261, 13381, '<td valign="top">Wow, a beautiful droplet shot.  Very nice.</td>', 'Wow, a beautiful droplet shot.  Very nice.', '2003-10-29 17:04:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(466311, 44232, 6520, '<td valign="top">This is my kind of picture 9!</td>', 'This is my kind of picture 9!', '2003-10-29 17:06:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(466312, 43849, 12253, '<td valign="top">Good shot and composition.  I think Neatimage would help this in reducing the background noise in the sky.</td>', 'Good shot and composition.  I think Neatimage would help this in reducing the background noise in the sky.', '2003-10-29 17:06:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(466313, 43992, 12432, '<td valign="top">Original framing focusing  the attention on the hands and the harpist concentration. Sure it''s gracious and well expressed.</td>', 'Original framing focusing  the attention on the hands and the harpist concentration. Sure it''s gracious and well expressed.', '2003-10-29 17:07:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(466316, 44350, 12253, '<td valign="top">I like this shot a lot; I think I would have cropped the left a bit though, so as not to center the butterfly.</td>', 'I like this shot a lot; I think I would have cropped the left a bit though, so as not to center the butterfly.', '2003-10-29 17:07:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(466323, 43490, 12253, '<td valign="top">Very nice macro; I suggest cropping the right to eliminate the brighter background and a bit more of the bottom trunk, and thus apply the rule of thirds to make the compositon more powerful.</td>', 'Very nice macro; I suggest cropping the right to eliminate the brighter background and a bit more of the bottom trunk, and thus apply the rule of thirds to make the compositon more powerful.', '2003-10-29 17:10:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(466324, 44388, 12253, '<td valign="top">Excellent flower shot with good natural symmetry.  A bit more DOF would have help some.</td>', 'Excellent flower shot with good natural symmetry.  A bit more DOF would have help some.', '2003-10-29 17:11:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(466325, 44122, 12253, '<td valign="top">Good exposure.  Was this taken during the challenge dates?  Where is there snow already?</td>', 'Good exposure.  Was this taken during the challenge dates?  Where is there snow already?', '2003-10-29 17:12:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(466326, 44318, 13342, '<td valign="top">This picture is absolutely perfect. I love the way the sun is coming through on the ground and trees. Perfect timing. A very peacefull, "gracefull" mood.</td>', 'This picture is absolutely perfect. I love the way the sun is coming through on the ground and trees. Perfect timing. A very peacefull, "gracefull" mood.', '2003-10-29 17:13:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(466327, 44318, 12253, '<td valign="top">Beautiful color  and graceful forms.  A lovely shot.</td>', 'Beautiful color  and graceful forms.  A lovely shot.', '2003-10-29 17:14:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(466329, 43794, 12253, '<td valign="top">Nice composition, I think a softer light might have been good here.  The reflections and shine of the skin seems distractive here.</td>', 'Nice composition, I think a softer light might have been good here.  The reflections and shine of the skin seems distractive here.', '2003-10-29 17:15:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(466330, 44416, 10260, '<td valign="top">I really like this photo.....grace in the deepest meaning.  I''ve seen the salmon spawning in Alaska, going to the greatest hardship to make it to give life, and then die. 10</td>', 'I really like this photo.....grace in the deepest meaning.  I''ve seen the salmon spawning in Alaska, going to the greatest hardship to make it to give life, and then die. 10', '2003-10-29 17:16:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(466333, 43865, 12432, '<td valign="top">Three times gracious indeed. Also very well framed and sharp image. I like the two color making the whole shot very attractive.</td>', 'Three times gracious indeed. Also very well framed and sharp image. I like the two color making the whole shot very attractive.', '2003-10-29 17:20:47.000000', NULL, 1),
