(473044, 44110, 12589, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by KING:</b></div><hr/><i>The composition is good but I think the focus is very soft (perhaps too soft for my liking). This image could also use some more light (just a little to increase the ''whiteness'' of the white).</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You''re right!  But the focus was nearly ok. I have problems when trying to make from the original photo the required sized one..:( <br/>Whenever I rescale the photo I loose quality. I didn''t find yet the right procedure. In order to reach the 150kB I must save it whit less aquracy. I wonder how others do this..</td>', 'Originally posted by KING:The composition is good but I think the focus is very soft (perhaps too soft for my liking). This image could also use some more light (just a little to increase the ''whiteness'' of the white).  You''re right!  But the focus was nearly ok. I have problems when trying to make from the original photo the required sized one..:( Whenever I rescale the photo I loose quality. I didn''t find yet the right procedure. In order to reach the 150kB I must save it whit less aquracy. I wonder how others do this..', '2003-11-05 03:51:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(473168, 44318, 12796, '<td valign="top">see ratings 1, 2 and 3 for this image! This is a clear indication that we must weed out people.. Is this because they dont know what a good photograph is or is it just under rating only because they too have submitted an image in the challenge! I''ve seen so many under rating in this site!</td>', 'see ratings 1, 2 and 3 for this image! This is a clear indication that we must weed out people.. Is this because they dont know what a good photograph is or is it just under rating only because they too have submitted an image in the challenge! I''ve seen so many under rating in this site!', '2003-11-05 05:48:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(473169, 44309, 8522, '<td valign="top">Thanks to those of you that liked this... it''s still one of my lowest scoring pics though. The unusual effect came from a curves adjustment that made the mid-shadows brighter than the mid-highlights. Also lots of runs though NeatImage, and some extreme colour balancing.</td>', 'Thanks to those of you that liked this... it''s still one of my lowest scoring pics though. The unusual effect came from a curves adjustment that made the mid-shadows brighter than the mid-highlights. Also lots of runs though NeatImage, and some extreme colour balancing.', '2003-11-05 05:49:06.000000', NULL, 0),
