(473248, 44309, 8522, '<td valign="top">All NeatImage does is remove noise. As a result of using it 3 times for this image, it has the result of losing a lot of detail, and giving an unusual blurred look. The main reason though, is that after the curves and colour adjustments there was tons of noise.<br/>The photo really didn''t look far off the finished DPC entry after opening it in Photoshop and applying the curves adjustment. That is what resulted in the strong sky colours, as it was taken at sunset, and quite a nice one at that.</td>', 'All NeatImage does is remove noise. As a result of using it 3 times for this image, it has the result of losing a lot of detail, and giving an unusual blurred look. The main reason though, is that after the curves and colour adjustments there was tons of noise.The photo really didn''t look far off the finished DPC entry after opening it in Photoshop and applying the curves adjustment. That is what resulted in the strong sky colours, as it was taken at sunset, and quite a nice one at that.', '2003-11-05 07:34:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(473249, 44223, 11284, '<td valign="top">Thank you!<br/>Though some critical words would have been helpfull. :)<br/> <br/>Instead of picturing the permormance (action takes place in an Opera and Ballet theatre) i show the hidden part, the preparation.<br/>In that grace-producing house there are ~20 cleaners, who earn 5$ per day. So, with a taste of irony you see the dance of a cleaner in the surreal world of grace.</td>', 'Thank you!Though some critical words would have been helpfull. :) Instead of picturing the permormance (action takes place in an Opera and Ballet theatre) i show the hidden part, the preparation.In that grace-producing house there are ~20 cleaners, who earn 5$ per day. So, with a taste of irony you see the dance of a cleaner in the surreal world of grace.', '2003-11-05 07:37:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(473261, 44318, 472, '<td valign="top">great lines willem.</td>', 'great lines willem.', '2003-11-05 07:51:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(473267, 44318, 4482, '<td valign="top">Very gracefull. Good job!</td>', 'Very gracefull. Good job!', '2003-11-05 07:57:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(473270, 43649, 6870, '<td valign="top">Thanks for your kind comments, everyone. For the record, I tried this using the rule of thirds, and it just didn''t work. For the mythic effects I was aiming for, centered was really the only choice. As you can imagine, I took about a hundred or more shots (oops--hyperbole there!) of this until I got it right. I had intended to have more ground, with the horizon in the upper third, but alas, I could not get the camera 12 feet into the air for this effect--I kept sinking into the salty mud as it was! I think Zeuszen''s and dr. Rick''s comments below sum up what I was trying to do.<br/> <br/>Congrats to the winners--well deserved, I say!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-11-05 16:06:48.</i></td>', 'Thanks for your kind comments, everyone. For the record, I tried this using the rule of thirds, and it just didn''t work. For the mythic effects I was aiming for, centered was really the only choice. As you can imagine, I took about a hundred or more shots (oops--hyperbole there!) of this until I got it right. I had intended to have more ground, with the horizon in the upper third, but alas, I could not get the camera 12 feet into the air for this effect--I kept sinking into the salty mud as it was! I think Zeuszen''s and dr. Rick''s comments below sum up what I was trying to do. Congrats to the winners--well deserved, I say!', '2003-11-05 08:01:44.000000', '2003-11-05 16:06:48.000000', 0),
(473276, 44318, 6870, '<td valign="top">Absolutely stunning image! Well done and congratulations on the ribbon!</td>', 'Absolutely stunning image! Well done and congratulations on the ribbon!', '2003-11-05 08:04:37.000000', NULL, 0),
